      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): read Ephesians 4:26 and James 1:19 aloud \u2014 notice the ORDER built into both. | The big idea (10): body first, recognition second, choice third \u2014 the flinch is the alarm, not the verdict, and the first story must be searched. | Go deeper (10): walk Elijah\u2019s flinch (1 Kings 19:3-8) \u2014 the flight, the false story under the juniper tree, and heaven\u2019s body-first care; then practice the reset question and the space sentence together. | Reflect together (10): use the prompts; let people name their own flinch patterns without shame \u2014 the room should feel like the angel\u2019s meal, not a courtroom. | Take it with you (2): every person picks ONE trigger to run the three beats on this week \u2014 and says "Let me think about that" out loud once before leaving.',
