      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): read 2 Corinthians 2:11 and 4:2 aloud together \u2014 the know-them and the never-use-them, side by side. | The big idea (10): the five devices, each with its Bible case: the staircase (Delilah), the frame-shift (Eden), the novelty hook (Athens), the story-rails (Nathan \u2014 the righteous use), the speed play (Proverbs 7). | Go deeper (10): where do these arrive in YOUR week \u2014 the feed, the sales call, the pressured ask, even church-flavored flattery or urgency; practice the four-question shield out loud. | Reflect together (10): use the prompts; keep the tone pastoral \u2014 the goal is armor, not paranoia, and the established heart (Hebrews 13:9) is the real defense. | Take it with you (2): each person names ONE incoming pressure they will slow down this week and says the sentence: "Let me pray and test this first."',
