      senior: 'For the seasoned believer, this lesson hands you the referee\u2019s whistle you have earned: you have lived through enough prophecy-panics \u2014 dates set and missed, antichrists named and buried \u2014 to teach the young what each cycle forgot. Hold the frameworks honestly: godly scholars have defended premillennialism (in both its post-tribulational and dispensational pre-trib forms), amillennialism, and postmillennialism; the four lenses on Revelation each answer real features of the text. You may hold your own position with conviction \u2014 many in this house\u2019s tradition expect a literal reign and a church that endures tribulation \u2014 while refusing the two sins the debate breeds: making a timeline a test of fellowship, and making a chart a substitute for the commands. Now the pastoral assignments. FIRST, calibrate the panic the way Paul did: the Thessalonians were already being shaken by day-has-arrived claims IN THE FIRST CENTURY (2 Thessalonians 2:1-3) \u2014 name that history; it inoculates. SECOND, weigh the viral timelines by the text: when a teacher maps the first seal\u2019s crown to corona, you may note gently and factually that the wordplay lives in Latin and English \u2014 Revelation\u2019s Greek word is stephanos, a victor\u2019s wreath \u2014 and the text itself (Revelation 6:2) names a bow, a given crown, and conquest, nothing more; when a living man is named as the second beast, the reticence rule holds (L22): teach what is written and stop. THIRD, honor what the enduring-tribulation teachers get pastorally RIGHT: a church prepared to suffer loses nothing if it is spared, but a church promised escape and met by fire can shipwreck \u2014 so build saints who can endure (the L22 watch) while holding the blessed hope with both hands (Titus 2:13); prepared-and-hoping is the posture that cannot be embarrassed. FOURTH, keep the purposes sovereign: prophecy was given to comfort (1 Thessalonians 4:18) and purify (1 John 3:2-3; 2 Peter 3:14) \u2014 the teacher who wields it to terrify and to sell has inverted it, whatever his chart. And model the gaze the angels corrected: "why stand ye gazing up into heaven?" (Acts 1:11) \u2014 He is coming in like manner, certainly; until then the power is for WITNESS (Acts 1:8). Even so, come, Lord Jesus (Revelation 22:20) \u2014 prayed by saints in every camp for two thousand years, and answered soon enough for all of them.',
